<title>SINGAPORE: SIA 1st-half load-factor falls.</title>
<headline>SIA 1st-half load-factor falls.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore Airlines Ltd (SIA) said on Monday its operating details for the six months to September 30, 1996 were as follows:</p>
<p>    Capacity tonne-km (bln)	     6.60 vs   5.98</p>
<p>    Load tonne-km (bln)		   4.63 vs   4.16</p>
<p>    Overall load factor (percent)    70.2  vs   69.6</p>
<p>    Available seat-km (bln)	    36.15 vs  33.55</p>
<p>    Revenue passenger-km (bln)	 27.20 vs  24.44</p>
<p>    Passenger seat factor (percent)  75.2  vs   72.8</p>
<p>    Cargo capacity tonne-km (bln)     3.00 vs   2.61</p>
<p>    Cargo load tonne-km (bln)	   2.02 vs   1.80</p>
<p>    Cargo load factor (percent)	67.3  vs   68.9</p>
<p>    Passengers carried (million)	5.93 vs   5.38</p>
<p>    Cargo carried (million kg)	320.9  vs  290.5</p>
<p>    Yield (cents):     overall	 66.4  vs   71.2</p>
<p>			     passenger     94.3  vs  100.4</p>
<p>			     cargo	   31.0  vs   33.6</p>
<p>    Unit cost (cents)		    43.4  vs   44.4</p>
<p>    Breakeven load factor		65.4  vs   62.4</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
</text>
